s to find it looks like we're going  to have some new armor pieces available  to us hidden in treasure chests placed  around Hyrule well Nintendo never said  this would be easy in addition to the  correct masks that will assist us in  finding hidden seeds by vibrating when  there's one nearby  there's headgear from both Majora's Mask  and Twilight Princess a full gear set  from Phantom Hourglass  and wait is that is that oh god stop the  presses  cancel all my meetings and forget the  rest of this DLC the tingle  is all I need in my life oh there  there's still more features fine we'll  do that but that's right back to tingle  okay ah anyway  Nintendo hasn't said exactly what the  gear will do or if they'll even do  anything at all but I'd love to see  something Moon related with Majora's  Mask like every time you put it on it  will cause a Blood Moon to rise the  Minda helmet is a little bit more  complicated because she has so many  different powers but maybe even  something like a locator for treasures  like they do with the shrines would be  cool the phantom armor could be a  defense heavy set I mean just look at it  it's all as a rock right and the tingle  outfit aside from making every single  one of us uncomfortably excited could  have some cool perks like more selfie  poses or an increased rupee draw or even  a fairy detector the sky's the limit  would tingle it's anyone's guess as to  what they will actually do but I'll give  you the Tendo the benefit of the doubt  and hopefully we'll be treated to some  awesome new abilities with this gear  there's also a mode included in this DLC  called heroes path it's kind of a nifty  addition as it tracks links location and  movement throughout Hyrule over the last  200 hours played but that's kind of it I  guess it's kind of cool if you like  seeing where you've been and where you  haven't Nintendo seems to be touting  this as a way to help people find more  shrines in the game but what about those  who have already 